<title>UK: BAA ranks U.S. top for its UK air imports/e.</title>
<headline>BAA ranks U.S. top for its UK air imports/e.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the top origin and destination for air cargo imports and exports through BAA Plc airports during April to December 1996, an unchanged ranking from the same period a year earlier, BAA figures show.</p>
<p>BAA does not publish a tonnage breakdown by country of exports or imports from its airports which handled a total 1.17 million tonnes in Apr-Dec last year, a rise of 5.2 percent on the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Canada maintained its second ranking in both years for imports. The order for the top seven export markets was unchanged from Apr-Dec 1995 with Japan staying in second place.</p>
<p>Air Cargo Exports ex-BAA airports with total in tonnes</p>
<p> Rank			    Apr-Dec 96	     Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p> 1				     U.S.		   U.S.</p>
<p> 2				     Japan		  Japan</p>
<p> 3				     Canada		 Canada</p>
<p> 4				     Germany		Germany</p>
<p> 5				     Hong Kong	    Hong Kong</p>
<p> 6				     Singapore	    Singapore</p>
<p> 7				     Australia	    Australia</p>
<p> 8				     S.Africa	     India</p>
<p> 9				     UAE		    Italy</p>
<p> 10				    India		  France</p>
<p>Export tonnage all countries   560,047		531,947</p>
<p>Air Cargo Imports into BAA airports with total in tonnes  Rank			    Apr-Dec 96	   Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p> 1				     U.S.		   U.S.</p>
<p> 2				     Canada		 Canada</p>
<p> 3				     Japan		  Germany</p>
<p> 4				     Germany		Japan</p>
<p> 5				     Singapore	    Hong Kong</p>
<p> 6				     Hong Kong	    Israel</p>
